---
title: Chicken Salan
description: this is a basic chicken curry that is made at home. My son loves it and if you have the ingredients it really is a less than 45 min recipe
---

Get all your ingredients together.

Add @fried onion{1%tablespoon}, @garlic paste{1%teaspoon}, @ginger paste{1%teaspoon}, @red chili powder{1/2%teaspoon}, @turmeric{1/2%teaspoon}, @ground cumin{1/2%teaspoon}, and @ground coriander{1/2%teaspoon} to a #pan with @oil{} and a little @water{}. Add @salt{} to taste. Cook for ~{3-5%minutes}. Add @water{} as needed to not burn.

Add @chicken{1/2} and @potato{1} and cook for ~{15-20%minutes} until the kushboo (good smell) comes and the chicken and potatoes have melded with the masala. Add @water{} as needed so it doesn't burn and @oil{} as needed so it fries. Add @salt{} to taste and stir frequently.

Add @tomato sauce{1/2%cup} and cook for ~{5%minutes}.

Add @water{} until the @chicken{} and @potato{} are covered. Cover with a #lid and cook until the meat is done and the potatoes are soft.
